--TEST--
A compiler-recognized attribute on a declaration where it builds nothing is `E0874` at the attribute: a command on a class or a property, a route on a property, an API description on a class, and a JSON derive on a method
--FILE--
<?nvs
#[Core\Command(name: "report")]
#[Core\Api(tags: ["shop"])]
class Shop {
    #[Core\Command(name: "count")]
    #[Core\Route(path: "/count", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    public int $count = 0;

    #[Core\Json\Derive]
    public function total(): int {
        return $this->count;
    }
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0874]: `Core\Command` is used on a class, and its declaration allows only `method`
  --> case.nvs:2:3
%A
error[E0874]: `Core\Api` is used on a class, and its declaration allows only `method`
  --> case.nvs:3:3
%A
error[E0874]: `Core\Command` is used on a property, and its declaration allows only `method`
  --> case.nvs:5:7
%A
error[E0874]: `Core\Route` is used on a property, and its declaration allows only `method`
  --> case.nvs:6:7
%A
error[E0874]: `Core\Json\Derive` is used on a method, and its declaration allows only `class`
  --> case.nvs:9:7
%A
